; Evidence labels:
; VERIFIED-BYTES: directly read from this SHA-256-locked image.
; STATIC-DECODE: instruction meaning decoded from a documented entry/state.
; RUNTIME-EMULATOR: reproduced in the pinned Snes9x core; record input injection.
; REPORTED: user observation or reference; not yet reproduced here.
; CANDIDATE: lead needing caller/data-flow/runtime evidence.
; UNKNOWN: unresolved. Never assign invented addresses to roadmap features.
; Feature status: PLANNED / RESEARCH / IMPLEMENTED / VALIDATED.
; IMPLEMENTED does not imply runtime validation or release acceptance.
; Observed zero/$FF runs are not certified free space. Preserve unknown bytes.
; Each patch must document feature ID, original bytes, replacement bytes, caller,
; register widths, DBR/DP/stack assumptions, return, clobbers, and validation.
