;   $CE46 copies 53 input bytes from $084E-$0882 to $0883-$08B7.
;   $D1F0 classifies input: $00 normal, $01 preset, $02 error, $03 extra mode.
;   $00 -> $D14E symbol decode -> $D1D0 zero expansion -> $CE54 checksum.
;   Compare DP $00/$01/$02 to $0896/$0897/$0898; reject mismatch OR zero sum.
;   On success call $D00B (unpack live state), then JSL $06:8028.
;   $01 -> JSL $06:8028 without normal decoding.
;   $02 -> sound $60, $CE78 message/old-code handling, retry or preset success.
;   $03 -> immediate RTS; outer $C813 repeats after returning from extra mode.
;   Successful normal/preset path requests sound $34/$22 respectively and
;   returns A=$00. $06:8028 calls $00:84DC, preserves $0420, sets $F3,
;   calls $00:84DC twice in an X=2 loop, restores $0420 and RTL. Exact renderer
;   semantics still UNKNOWN; successful world entry is reproduced in P10.
; $01:B76B-$B784 subsequently calls $02:DADE, $02:DD22 (X=0, and X=$0A if
; $10C8 nonzero), then $02:8B87. These are resume/reconstruction dependencies.
; $02:DF09 (PC $015F09) is a verified JSL $03:D662 generation call site.
; $02:DF06-$DF26 points $17C3-$17C5 at $00:0883 for display afterwards.
; $03:D662-$D688: PHP; SEP #$30; PHB; PHK; PLB; $D689 pack; $CE54 checksum;
; store checksum to $0896-$0898; $D7DE zero removal; $D825 five-bit packing;
; $D896 prefix/glyph/display formatting; PLB; PLP; RTL.
