; 03C. STARTUP AND INTERRUPT CONTEXT -- FASTROM PREREQUISITES, 2026-10-11
; ============================================================================
; VERIFIED-BYTES / STATIC-DECODE. No FastROM patch or timing result in this pass.
; WRAM clear $00:8C69-$8CDD / PC $000C69-$000CDD:
; PHP/REP #$30; A=0, X=$0100. Decrement X by two, store 16-bit zero at
; $0200+X through $1F00+X, loop to X=0: clears mirror $0200-$1FFF.
; TSX/DEX then descending 16-bit stores at $0000+X, followed by STA $0000,
; clear the area below the live stack frame. PLP/RTS preserve active frames.
; In reset's established S=$01FF context, JSR and PHP leave S=$01FC;
; stores clear $0000-$01FC, retaining $01FD status and $01FE-$01FF return.
; This is not a reusable whole-WRAM clear without considering stack context.
; $1084..$10F3 and indexed flags $1800..$181F are cleared on this cold path.
; Therefore password unpack's sticky flags in P12 differ from a cold startup;
; SRAM restore must follow initialization and deliberately define owned bytes.
;
; Startup tail $00:EFBD-$EFE6:
; A8=1 -> $4200; A=0 -> $4016,$420B,$420C,$420D. The $420D store is
; $00:EFCF / PC $006FCF, bytes 8D 0D 42. Native startup explicitly selects
; SlowROM. Whole-file byte search found one absolute STA $420D signature;
; data matches/other addressing forms require control-flow review, so this
; does not prove there are no other effective writes anywhere in the engine.
; $00:EFD2 reads $7FF000; zero calls $00:EFEA, then writes $FF to $7FF000.
; Reset prefix sets this byte zero. $EFEA-$EFFF saves P, selects A8, sets
; DP $00..$02 to source $0A:8250, SEI/JSR $F066/CLI/PLP/RTL.
; Port-based transfer code identifies this as the startup audio upload guard;
; full payload format, transfer contract and re-entry behavior remain pending.
; $00:EFE2 SEP #$30; $EFE4 JMP [$EFE7]; $EFE7-$EFE9 is data 00 80 01,
; destination $01:8000. Those pointer bytes must not be decoded as opcodes.
;
; Native IRQ $00:8E41-$8E68 / PC $000E41-$000E68:
; PHP/SEP #$30/PHA; acknowledge $4211; write $212C=4,$212D=0;
; DP $50/$51 -> successive $2111 writes, $52/$53 -> successive $2112 writes;
; PLA/PLP/RTI. No DBR/DP establishment or save, no X/Y arithmetic. Handler
; requires foreground DBR to make absolute WRAM/MMIO addresses appropriate;
; DP-dependent scroll shadows are inherited. P restoration returns caller widths.
;
; Native NMI $00:8E69-$8F72 / PC $000E69-$000F72:
; REP #$30/PHP/PHA/PHY/PHX/PHB/PHD/SEP #$20/PHK/PLB sets DBR=00,
; saves wide A/X/Y and DBR/DP. It does NOT set DP; direct-page shadows depend
; on inherited DP. $2100=$80, acknowledge $4210, interrupt shadow $BA ->
; $4200; pending DMA mask $78 -> $420B, HDMA shadows $78/$79 -> $420C.
; PPU shadows are copied; SEP #$10 selects X8 for audio-command lookup:
; $0420 indexes explicit long-address table $0A:8220,X (when X<$F0),
; optional JSR $89AE at $8EDE, then $0420..$0423 -> $2140..$2143.
; REP #$10/REP #$20 precede these dispatches, in order (all JSR bank00
; except the explicitly long call; caller entry widths do not prove callee exit):
; $9FBE,$93C2,$8F73,$9259,$9AE5,$9186,$9323,$99C4,$9A36,$8FAB,
; $8FCE,$907A,$90B6,$9126,$913A,$9039,$9AD1,$8FF6,
; JSL $00:9A0F, JSR $9AA9.
; $8F43 SEP #$20; restore HDMA/display/interrupt shadows, set DP $9F bit7,
; write color shadows $73..$75 -> $2132; $8F6A REP #$20;
; PLD/PLB/PLX/PLY/PLA/PLP/RTI. The local PHP records widths after REP;
; hardware interrupt's earlier saved P is restored by RTI, including original
; caller M/X. Do not infer lost caller widths solely from the first REP/PHP.
;
; FastROM experiment dependencies now have concrete addresses: startup $420D,
; long game-entry pointer, vector targets, interrupt-local JSRs, explicit
; $0A:8220 audio table, and PHK/PLB-derived DBR. Mirrored entry changes PHK's
; bank value; relocation must account for bank-local code/data reads and the
; inherited IRQ DBR/NMI DP contracts. Remaining dispatch bodies and long-call
; inventory still need audit. No free space or replacement hook certified here.
;
