; NMI PUBLICATION AND FOREGROUND ACKNOWLEDGMENT
; NMI03C calls $00:9AA9: PHP/SEP30, increment DP $95; wrap increments $96.
; It then services conditional effect timers $0455+X and restores P/RTS.
; $95-$96 is therefore a16-bit NMI-service counter in this context, also used
; elsewhere for phase/random variation;512 low-byte/high-byte wrap cases pass.
; $00:8F57-$8F59 sets DP $9F bit7 near NMI end (after dispatch and display
; restore, before final color stores/register restore). It publishes completion.
; Word DP $9E includes that completion bit15 and other work/control flags.
; $00:8520 sets word flags by OR; $00:8529 saves P/DBR, PHK/PLB, then
; $852D EOR #FFFF / AND $9E / STA $9E clears bits selected by input A16.
; Returns DBR/P restored;44 set +44 clear selected cases pass.
; General $00:84DC-$8501 saves P/DBR, sets DBR00, enables shadow $BA bits$81
; into $4200, selects A16. If $9E negative, clears old completion with mask8000;
; polls $84F8 until new bit15 appears, then clears8000 and returns via $852D.
; Thus this is a fresh-completion wait in normal interrupt-enabled operation,
; not merely a busy delay with a fixed instruction count. X/Y not used locally.
; Foreground $01:8260-$828C checks byte $009F bit7, optionally acknowledges old
; work and (if $1108 negative) calls $05:E797 -> $8A58 before polling $8273.
; After completion calls $828D, clears $10DA, increments $1053, returns request.
; $828D acknowledgment chooses mask0080 only when the16-bit value at $1107
; has bit15 set, queue $066F=0 and ($9E & $7FFF)=0; otherwise8080. PHX/PHP
; are restored after $00:8529 call.36 policy cases stop before that long call.
; Small mask0080 leaves completion bit15 set deliberately; do not rewrite as
; unconditional frame flag clear. Full semantic ownership of other bits pending.
;
; EXPLORATION LOOP VARIANTS
; $04:8086-$80F6 / PC $020086-$0200F6 begins SEI, calls $01:8260.
; Nonzero result routes $8068's input/exit handling; zero proceeds through
