; 03J. FRAME-PATH BANK DEPENDENCIES AND INDIRECT DISPATCH -- 2026-10-11
; ============================================================================
; Scope: the12 selected ranges in03I, not the entire reachable call graph.
; Build/audit_frame_banks.py records33 distinct explicit JSL destinations in
; Research/frame_bank_audit_results.json, with callers, physical offsets and
; entry bytes. All33 destinations explicitly name low banks00/01/04/05/06/1F.
; Entering the game through a high-bank alias alone will not retarget these
; calls. This is an address inventory, not a measured time/speedup estimate.
;
; ENTRY BANK POLICY -- BODY CONTRACTS MUST BE AUDITED SEPARATELY
; Two entries ($00:84DC,$00:8529) begin PHP/PHB/PHK/PLB; tails reviewed03I.
; Three balanced wrappers save DBR, PHK/PLB, JSR body, restore DBR, RTL:
; $06:834D -> $8455; $06:8355 -> $84C6; $06:83A5 -> $B54F.
; Eighteen entries are JSR-body/RTL shims without an entry DBR establishment.
; Ten other entries require individual flow/body analysis. JSON lists each one.
; A shim does not imply its body leaves DBR unchanged: $06:8341 -> $BA73 and
; $04:A205 -> $A209 establish their own bank with PHB/PHK/PLB. $06:B54F also
; saves/establishes DBR before calling $B557 and restoring it on return.
; PHK/PLB derives data bank from executing code bank; a high-bank entry changes
; that value. PLB updates N/Z, including when restoring DBR. These wrappers
; are not blanket flag-preserving contracts. The combat callers after $06:834D
; and $06:8355 use AND #00FF at $05:89FD/$8A1D to refresh their result flags.
; $06:C220 -> $C224 calls $C230, then explicit JSL $06:8341; $06:C22C calls
; $C230 alone. The nested sprite preparation/wait is therefore also reachable
; through the exploration/update paths; do not audit only the top combat call.
;
; ACTOR TABLE DISPATCH -- ROM DATA BANK AND JUMP CODE BANK ARE DISTINCT
; $06:8510-$8537 / PC $030510-$030537 reads actor type $1330,X, doubles it
; in A8, and selects the normal directory path for resulting Y >= $20.
; Reads $8550,Y/$8551,Y through DBR into DP $8C-$8D; takes $1338,X & $1F,
; doubles it, reads two handler bytes via ($8C),Y into $008A-$008B, then
; $8535 JMP ($008A). The pointer is read in bank00; the near jump retains PBR.
; The actor-pass wrappers above establish DBR06 before the normal dispatch.
; Tested types $19/$1E both select pointer $863A, from $8582/$858C respectively.
; The28 contiguous words $863A-$8671 precede the first handler at $8672:
; 8672 8830 8844 886D 8880 88AF 88FF 895C 896F 89B6 8A0C 8A14 8AB4 8AF2
; 8B7A 8BA6 8BE6 8CD6 8D5F 8D75 8E1F 8E8A 8ED1 8F0B 8F46 8FA2 8FF9 9085
; Mask $1F permits indices28-31 too, but those read handler instruction bytes
; as words ($3822,$0581,$FF29,$78D0). This is not a bounds check or evidence
; that those states are legally reached; other actor types remain unclassified.
; 896 bounded original-instruction checks PASSED: types19/1E, states0-27,
; eight combinations of upper state bits, fixed PBR=DBR06 and PBR=DBR86.
; Checks compare both table pointer and extracted handler, STOP before JMP.
; AliasCPU models only mirrored ROM and low RAM with fixed equal PBR/DBR.
; It cannot validate inherited/mismatched DBR, actual bank transitions, handler
; execution, interrupts, MMIO or timing. No high-bank ROM patch was executed.
;
; INLINE RETURN-ADDRESS DISPATCH -- NOT AN ORDINARY RETURNING SUBROUTINE
; $05:E776-$E792 / PC $02E776-$02E792 saves Y in DP $C7, doubles A, uses
; the stacked JSR return address as table base ($C5-$C6), and reads its selected
; word at base +2*A+1. PHK/PLB establishes DBR05 without saving incoming DBR.
; It restores Y, then JMP ($00C5): consumes the JSR return word and tail-jumps
; within current PBR, leaving DBR equal to the code bank. Full caller stack and
; eventual exit contracts remain open; the bounded harness does not test this.
; Confirmed caller $05:821C loads $10D8; $821F JSR $E776; inline words at
; $8222-$8229 are $822A,$82BE,$82F5,$8333. This data must not be decoded as
; instructions. It is reached through $05:E79B and the combat request6 path.
; Other raw JSR-byte matches at PC $028268,$0282E7,$02830B,$02BFD0 are candidate
; sites only here; no full caller/selector/table or stack proof for those sites.
;
; ADDRESSING RULES / FIRST-CONVERSION IMPLICATIONS
; Near jumps keep PBR; ordinary absolute data reads use DBR. JMP (a) reads its
; pointer from bank00; JMP/JSR (a,X) reads its table in PBR. Thus the scene
; dispatcher $01:815B's JMP ($8163,X) follows a code-bank alias, while the actor
; dispatch first needs correct DBR for ROM table reads. Do not rewrite every
; two-byte pointer as though it contained a bank, or assume PHK/PLB harmless.
; Primary reference: WDC W65C816S datasheet, addressing and section7.9:
; https://www.westerndesigncenter.com/wdc/documentation/w65c816s.pdf
; Indexed-indirect PBR-table behavior corroborated by upstream Snes9x source:
; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/snes9xgit/snes9x/master/cpuaddr.h
; This source check is not verification of every instruction in the pinned DLL.
; Before a conversion, select a narrow path and finish its callee data/MMIO,
; DBR/DP, indirect destination, width/stack and interrupt audits. Preserve03I's
; handshake and phase waits; compare against natural fixtures. Entry categories
; and896 table checks do not establish a complete FastROM-ready path.
;
