; 03K. NMI DISPLAY CONSUMERS, DMA SETUP AND NARROW WAIT AUDIT -- 2026-10-11
; ============================================================================
; Eight bounded NMI leaves mapped below. Entry DBR/DP inherited from03C's NMI;
; PHP/SEP or REP establishes local widths and PLP restores entry P. None of
; these eight leaves establishes DBR or calls another routine. A/X/Y may be
; clobbered; the outer NMI saves them. This is not the complete NMI call graph.
;
; WORK FLAG CONSUMERS -- WORD $9E, BYTE MASKS UNLESS NOTED
; $00:8FAB-$8FCD mask0002: $77->$2130,$72->$2131,$6E->$212C,$6F->$212D;
; TRB clears byte bit1 after writing. Other bits, including high byte, retained.
; $00:8FCE-$8FF5 mask0004: $77->$2130,$72->$2131,$73/$74/$75->$2132;
; TRB clears byte bit2 after writing. The three fixed-color writes keep order.
; $00:9126-$9139 mask0020: $45->$2106, then TRB clears byte bit5.
; $00:913A-$9185 mask0001: $58->$211A, pairs $59-$64->$211B-$2120.
; This routine DOES NOT clear bit0: persistent Mode7 register refresh while set.
; $00:9039-$9079 always copies $48-$53 in pairs to $210D-$2112 (scroll).
; $00:907A-$90B5 always copies $65-$6D->$2123-$212B and $70/$71->$212E/$212F.
; Source-shadow meanings derive from register destinations; ownership/acquisition
; of each flag and all other $9E bits remain open. Do not clear them wholesale.
;
; OAM TRANSFER -- WORD BIT0100 IS A SUPPRESSION FLAG
; $00:8F73-$8FAA tests word $9E &0100; if set, no register writes. Flag retained.
; Otherwise $2102-$2103=0000; configures DMA0, disables HDMA via $420C=0,
; starts DMA with $420B=1. Final channel0 setup before trigger:
; $4300=00,$4301=04,$4302-$4303=0200,$4304=00,$4305-$4306=0220.
; This selects a544-byte bank00:$0200 RAM source for $2104, not a ROM pointer
; derived from PHK. A code-bank alias does not imply changing that source bank.
; A16 STZ $4300 writes $4300 AND $4301; STA #2104->$4301 temporarily writes
; $4302=21; STA #0200->$4302 replaces it. A16 STZ $4304 also writes $4305,
; then STA #0220->$4305 replaces it. Preserve widths/byte order, not merely
; the apparent single-register operands. Trace records all14 byte writes.
;
; PENDING DMA CHANNEL MASK / PRECONFIGURED CHANNEL DEPENDENCIES
; $00:9FBE-$9FF5 starts DP $21=04,X=0; discards low two bits of DP $D2 and
; walks its bits2-7. For selected channel n=2..7, reads its3-byte record at
; DP $D3+3*(n-2): VMAIN byte, VRAM address low/high. Writes address to
; $2116/$2117, VMAIN to $2115, $420C=0, then $420B=1<<n, in ascending order.
; Clears entire byte $D2 afterward, including the ignored low two bits.
; Does NOT configure channel source bank/address/count here; those preexisting
; DMA registers are additional dependencies for a complete transfer audit.
; Do not infer that every selected transfer reads ROM or is accelerated by alias.
;
; BOUNDED VALIDATION / LIMITS
; Build/verify_nmi_transfers.py:8730 passing cases, nmi_transfer_results.json.
; Four flag consumers: all256 low bytes x four high bytes x two fixed banks
; =2048 cases each. OAM:five flag words x two banks=10; pending DMA:all256
; masks x two banks=512; unconditional scroll/window:four M/X widths x two
; banks=eight cases each. Bank models use PBR=DBR00/80 and DP0; original bytes.
; Check ordered byte writes, flags, restored P and balanced abstract leaf stack.
; No PPU/DMA effects, latches, bus read trace, interrupt entry/RTI or cycles
; simulated. Base harness pre-reads store operands; dummy MMIO values are not
; real hardware reads. Equal fixed-bank results are not actual patched execution.
; Added TRB and direct-page indexed ALU/load/store handling to the leaf harness;
; existing630 password and21866 progression checks re-run as regression coverage.
; Upstream Snes9x map_System/map_lorom corroborates low RAM/MMIO mirrors at
; banks00-3F/80-BF and LoROM high-bit aliases; this is not pinned-DLL verification:
; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/snes9xgit/snes9x/master/memmap.cpp
; DMA interpretation corroborated against upstream implementation:
; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/snes9xgit/snes9x/master/dma.cpp
;
; NARROW GENERAL-WAIT CANDIDATE -- STATIC CONTRACT, NO TEST PATCH
; $00:84DC-$8501 and shared tail $852D-$8538 read/write DP $BA/$9E, with
; the sole absolute data write $4200. No ROM data table or indirect destination.
; Entry saves P/DBR, PHK/PLB, sets A8 then A16; tail restores DBR/P and RTL.
; X/Y untouched. The stale-completion path explicitly JSLs low-bank $00:8529;
; its nested P/DBR save restores the wait's DBR before the near tail jump.
; A hypothetical $80:84DC entry therefore has a bank-local $80:852D tail but
; still uses the original low-bank clear helper. Low/high MMIO mapping applies
; to $4200; interrupts remain required to publish completion at inherited DP.
; IRQ03C inherits foreground DBR: mirrors00/80 provide the same register space,
; but this does not certify arbitrary DBR values or nonzero-DP foreground work.
; Wait conversion would be a bounded bank/return diagnostic; the completion
; wait itself is not evidence of a useful performance improvement. No selected
; call site, trampoline, vector, ROM header or MEMSEL write changed this pass.
; Next dependency: remaining NMI transfer bodies and DMA source constructors,
; then choose an isolated test with an explicit byte/stack contract and baseline.
