; ============================================================================
; 03L. VRAM COMMAND STREAMS AND DMA SOURCE CONSTRUCTORS -- 2026-10-11
; ============================================================================
; Two different native stream formats; do not interchange their length units.
; Build/verify_vram_streams.py executes original bounded routines with synthetic
; buffers; Research/vram_stream_results.json records3858 passing cases and tables.
; Fixed PBR=DBR00/80, DP0; explicit long RAM sources00/80/7E for CPU stream.
; MMIO writes recorded without DMA/PPU effects; no interrupt, timing, legal-state
; or patched-alias proof. No source-bank crossing or malformed-stream tests.
;
; CPU VRAM STREAM $00:9194-$9258 / PC $001194-$001258
; Saves P/DBR, PHK/PLB, SEP30; all reads [$A7],Y use an explicit long pointer.
; If byte $A0 positive/nonzero, copy $A1-$A3->$A7-$A9; if zero or negative,
; use bank00:$0670 instead. This selection is independent of the code bank.
; Record: destination high byte, destination low byte, control byte, payload.
; High byte0 terminates; clears $066F/$0670, restores DBR/P, RTL. Does not clear
; $A0 itself. $9186 gates the call on word $9E bit0200 CLEAR; relies on caller
; A16. $9AE5's positive-$A0 branch also calls $9194 then clears $A0 afterward.
; Control low6 bits give count in units; zero means64. Bit6 repeats one unit;
; bit7 selects VMAIN. Mode ($44 &7)==7: unit=one byte, high destination byte
; adjusted by subtract80 modulo256, VMAIN=03 if bit7 else00, data->$2118 only.
; Other modes: unit=two bytes, VMAIN=81 if bit7 else80, low/high->$2118/$2119.
; Literal payload size=count*unit; repeat payload size=unit. Destination writes
; occur HIGH->$2117 then LOW->$2116. Low16 source pointer advances by header+
; consumed payload after each record; $A9 bank is not updated on that advance.
; Y8 reads are bounded in tested records; do not extrapolate bank-boundary safety.
; 3072 checks:all256 controls x two mode families x three explicit source banks
; x two executing banks. Six default-selection checks ($A0=00/80/FF x banks).
; All compare byte writes, final pointer, queue reset, retained $A0, P and stack.
;
; DMA VRAM STREAM $00:9323-$93C1 / PC $001323-$0013C1
; PHP/SEP30; runs only when byte $9E bit40 set. Uses DBR-local ($AA),Y at
; $07B1, not a long source. Record:VRAM high,VRAM low,control,payload; high0
; terminates and clears $07B0/$07B1, but DOES NOT clear $9E bit40.
; Control low6 bits give DMA BYTE count. Bit6 selects fixed A-bus source
; ($4300=08) and consumes one payload byte; otherwise $4300=00 and consumes
; count bytes. Bit7 selects VMAIN81 rather than80. Both write through $2119
; ($4301=19), unlike the CPU stream's alternating low/high ports.
; Source $4302-$4303 points to the record's payload in bank00 ($4304=0).
; Count $4305=low6 bits,$4306=0; disable HDMA then trigger DMA0 ($420B=1).
; Length0 therefore programs hardware count0000, not the CPU stream's64 units.
; No zero-length DMA fixture executed; cannot treat it as an empty transfer.
; 504 checks:two direction bits x repeat/literal x lengths1-63 x two banks;
; validate ordered setup writes, pointer advance, queue reset, retained flag/P.
;
; COMMON DMA DESCRIPTOR INSTALLER $00:8D2A-$8D5E
; Entry A8 channel index, seven bytes DP $BB-$C1:
; BB=DMAP,BC=BBAD,BD/BE=source low/high,BF=source bank,C0/C1=byte count.
; Saves P/DBR, PHK/PLB, SEP30, saves low Y; disables HDMA; ORs 1<<channel
; into DP $78; reads bank-local word table $8D5F-$8D6E =4300,4310,...,4370;
; copies all seven descriptor bytes via ($26),Y. Returns A8=$78 and restores
; Y/DBR/P. No DMA trigger here; caller must write $420B or NMI uses pending $78.
; X untouched. Original caller high A/Y values not promised by bounded harness.
; 48 checks:channels0-7 x masks00/55/FF x banks00/80; exact writes/mask/return.
; Channel bounds/acquisition beyond0-7 remain unchecked by native routine here.
;
; VRAM FILL DESCRIPTOR CONSTRUCTORS / NMI $00:9259-$931C
; Gate byte $9F bit08. Mode7 branch prepares VRAM0000,length4000 and calls
; $92B3 once; other branch uses ROM word table $931D-$9322 (4000,4800,5000),
; plus low nibble of DP $C2 times0400, then calls $92B3 and $92E6.
; Native table index derived from ($C2 >>3)-2 in Y8; legal $C2 bounds unresolved.
; $92B3 sets VMAIN00, descriptor [08,18,C3,00,00,countLo,countHi].
; $92E6 sets VMAIN80, descriptor [08,19,C4,00,00,00,04]. Both set VRAM address
; from DP $2F/$30 and call $00:8D2A with channel0, write returned mask->$420B,
; TRB that mask from pending $78. $9317 finally clears $9F bit08.
; These are fixed-source fills from bank00 RAM bytes $00C3/$00C4, NOT ROM
; $C300/$C400. Four helper checks stop before JSL; descriptor separately checked.
; Fill byte ownership and all-mode caller/stack behavior remain open.
;
; CATALOG DMA TRANSFERS $00:93C2-$94DC AND $94DD-$94EF
; Gate word $9E bit1000. Destructively shift32-bit pending mask $9A-$9D, one
; low bit per slot0-31. No transfer for unset slots; clears1000 when exhausted.
; Bank-local tables:32 VRAM word addresses $94F0-$952F; four byte lengths
; $9530-$9537 =0400,0800,1000,2000; four source triples $9538-$9543:
; 14:8000,0C:A000,0C:8000,0D:8000. Group transitions at slots16,28,30.
; Slots0-15 use selector byte $042F+slot plus bit(slot) of word $042D as
; selector bit8; read a3-byte entry from ROM directory $9544 +3*selector.
; Directory length/legal selector range not yet established. $94DD supplies
; VRAM destination and group byte length; pointer remains explicitly banked.
; Slots16-31 start with group source triple; selector $042F+slot advances by
; group length per iteration. On16-bit source overflow, add8000 and increment
; source bank, retaining LoROM upper-half addressing. Signed X8 DEX/BMI bounds
; matter; tested selectors0,1,4,16,32,128, not arbitrary selector semantics.
; DMA0 uses VMAIN80, destination table word, explicit source triple and length;
; slots0-29 DMAP01/BBAD18, slots30-31 DMAP00/BBAD19. Disable HDMA, trigger01.
; 224 complete bounded checks:one mask bit per fixture, slots0-15 selector0
; with $042D=0; slots16-31 six selectors; both banks. Check all setup writes,
; destructive mask exhaustion, retained other flags and restored P/stack.
; Source constructors preserve explicit bank bytes despite code-bank aliases;
; table fetches use DBR and byte copies use DMA registers. Keep these separate.
