; INTERRUPT COMMAND INTERPRETER $00:9AE5-$9FBD
; Entry PHP/PHB/PHK/PLB/SEP30. $A0=0 returns; positive $A0 calls $00:9194 then
; clears $A0 (03L). Negative $A0 uses the larger interpreter. If original bit6
; set, reads a two-byte VRAM position header via $9F6B and TRB-clears bits40/10
; of $A0. $9B0D decrements byte $AC; negative result proceeds, other results
; return. This is an8-bit signed gate, not an unbounded delay counter.
; Proceeding calls $00:8929 with $A4 (callee still open), sets VMAIN80 and
; $0833=20, loads stream index $0831 into Y8 and destination from DP $B0/$B1.
; Stream pointer $A1-$A3 is explicit long. FF terminates BEFORE opcode dispatch:
; clears $A0/$0831 and restores DBR/P/RTS. Positive bytes call $9F8C, then
; $30=1 and common scheduler $9B3A. Helper $9F8C performs attribute handling,
; JSL $00:8230 glyph lookup, and writes two tile words in distinct positions.
; Explicit long call remains bank00 under a code alias; full helper run untested.
; Common scheduler increments destination by $30, saves Y->$0831, copies
; $A5->$AC; $A6 bit20 or absence of $A0 bit20 ends this pass. Exact command
; cadence depends on these states; do not replace with a fixed per-frame rate.
;
; PRIMARY TABLE $9B87-$9B96 / INDEX ($command &70)>>3
; Group8->$9B97: lookup through explicit bank01:$B78D pointer directory.
; Group9->$9BE3: pointer low/high from next bytes, source bank=command low nibble.
; GroupA->$9C17: numeric formatting path; source/sign/width controls, bank-local
; decimal table $8221,X; complete numeric command semantics not yet validated.
; GroupB->$9D39: ORs (low2 command bits)<<6 into attribute byte $A6; advances Y.
; GroupC->$9D49 and groupD->$9D73: shared fixed-size rendering path, with groupC
; leading-zero handling. Full payload/acquisition and rendering effects open.
; GroupE->$9DBE: inline literal two-byte words, low nibble count;0 means16.
; Explicit source pointer formed from $A1-$A3 +Y+1; two bytes per scheduled
; word to $2118/$2119; advances stream Y past opcode+payload when complete.
; GroupF->$9E0F: secondary dispatch. Both JMP(a,X) tables follow current PBR.
; 254 primary-prefix checks stop before JMP:127 command bytes80-FE x two banks.
; Eight literal-word fixtures (counts1/2/15/16 x banks) stop before scheduler;
; validate all word writes, partial/full state and final stream index.
;
; SECONDARY TABLE $9E18-$9E37 / INDEX2*(command &0F)
; Slots0-F:9E38,9E49,9E6B,9E9F,9E9F,9E9F,9EA8,9EB6,
;          9EC6,9ECC,9ED6,9F1F,9F44,9F48,9F4C,9F6B.
; Static roles:0 copies position bytes->$0428-$042B then reads header;1 switches
; low16 stream pointer, saving continuation in $0426/$0427;2 short blank fill;
; 3/4/5 share following-byte blank count;6 restores saved position;7 restores
; continuation;8/9 clear/set $A6 bit7;A branches on controller mask and blink
; state;B changes delay/mode state;C/D/E advance row origin by0/20/40.
; SlotF table word exists, but normal FF reaches termination first; do not
; describe it as a normally dispatched opcode. Thirty prefix checks stop before
; JMP for F0-FE x two banks. These labels are static behavior, not a proven
; full script grammar. Branch/call nesting, numeric/fixed-size paths remain open.
; $9F6B reads VRAM high/low header, copies destination to row origin $B2/$B3,
; advances LOW16 stream pointer by Y+2, clears Y; source bank unchanged.
; Two header-carry checks, ten countdown cases, two bounded termination cases
; pass. Termination tests supply an abstract saved P/DBR stack, not hardware RTI.
;
; PALETTE COPY/TRANSFORM $00:9A36-$9AA8
; PHP/SEP20; byte $0835=0 skips. Otherwise X16=count, $0834 selects CGRAM
; starting address=selector*16; palette RAM source=$046F+selector*32.
; The A16 store to $2121 also writes the next byte to $2122 before color data.
; BIT $0834 tests bit6. Clear: write source low OR18, high OR63 to $2122.
; Set: form ((color &001F)>>1) | ((color &03C0)>>1) | ((color &7800)>>1),
; then write low/high to $2122. Clears $0835 afterward, restores P/RTS.
; These are distinct forced-bit and half-component transformations; neither is
; an unconditional unchanged-palette upload. No palette math changed here.
; 768 cases:selectors0/1/7/15/40/41/47/4F x counts0/1/2/16 x12 seeded color
; sequences x banks00/80; compare every byte write, request clear and P/stack.
; Selectors/counts synthetic, no legal acquisition or PPU latch behavior proof.
;
; AUDIO SOURCE SELECTION AND BLOCK PROTOCOL -- STATIC, NOT EMULATED
; NMI $8ECA guards command X<F0; long lookup $0A:8220,X, skipFF or unchanged
; $0846; otherwise store new value->$0846 and JSR $89AE. A8 is used as byte
; offset into explicit bank00:$89DA triplets; first two are $0A:A5DB/$01:CA4D
; (offsets0/3), immediately followed by code at $89E0. Prefix48 bytes at
; $0A:8220-$824F contains only00/03/FF. Wider command/table legal bounds are
; not established by X<F0; following lookup bytes are not classified here.
; $89AE saves DP00/01/02 and Y, constructs long source DP00..02, JSL $00:F025,
; restores Y and saved pointer. No PHK-derived source bank in those triplets.
; $F025 saves $0420, writes FF to $2140-$2143 AND $0420-$0423; calls $00:84DC
; TWICE before PHP/SEI, clears NMI-enable bit80 in $4200 via TRB, sends F2
; through $2140 and calls $F066. Restores enable with TSB80, CLI/PLP, restores
; original $0420 and RTL. Other command shadow bytes remain FF at this layer.
; This frame-wait-bearing path is reachable from the NMI's conditional audio
; call; interrupt nesting/acknowledgment context needs CPU traces. No deadlock
; or successful upload inferred merely from the static calls or dummy MMIO model.
; $F066 uses A/X/Y16 then A8/Y16, polls $2140-$2141 for BBAA with countdown
;2000. Block header via [$00],Y:16-bit byte count,16-bit SPC destination.
; Nonzero blocks transfer bytes via $2140-$2141 with per-byte acknowledgment;
; zero-count block sends destination/termination handshake. Short waits use10
; countdown; timeout path sends FFFF->$2142-$2143, delays100 iterations and
; retries initial handshake, up to three attempts, then returns. These are
; loop-count bounds, not measured wall-time or guaranteed upload success.
; Static supplied source headers:0A:A5DB length30CD destinationC000, then
; zero-length header at PC0556AC destination0500;01:CA4D length2E44 destination
; C000, then zero-length header at PC00F895 destination0000. Payload hashes in
; JSON. File arithmetic confirms headers only; no SPC disassembly/behavior proof.
; Upload source Y16/pointer/bank crossing and APU timing remain unaudited.
;
; Added BIT and BVS/BVC to limited leaf harness. Existing password, NMI transfer
; and VRAM stream suites re-run after extension. No gameplay/calculation/FastROM
; changes. Full NMI callee closure is still open, especially $8929 and the larger
