; STA $0846, then BEQ skips. Valid translated music codes in this table01-2C;
; their upload lookup therefore stays within03M's classified48-byte prefix.
; This closes the legal table range for this REQUEST TRANSLATOR, not for every
; possible direct write to $0420 or the NMI's broader X<F0 guard.
; Result bit7 SET: index3*(result &7F), read triple at explicit $0A:8100;
; each NONZERO byte replaces its corresponding $0421/$0422/$0423 shadow.
; Zero bytes preserve old values. Original word DP00 saved/restored internally.
; Direct inputFD sets $0420=FF only; FE sets $0421-$0423=FF only; FF sets all
; four toFF. No APU port writes here; NMI later copies command shadows to ports.
; PHX is after SEP30: preserves low X, not an arbitrary incoming X16 high byte.
; P restored at return; X8 entry used for tests. Y and A may be clobbered.
; 4096 cases:all256 requests x old command00/01/2C/FF x old set00/03 x banks
;00/80. Independent translation/triple model compares all shadows, DP00 word,
; return status/X for returning cases, or stops before $8958 JSR $89AE if needed.
; Upload-stop cases do not test eventual stack/return or audible effect behavior.
