; NUMERIC COMMAND FORMATTER $00:9CAA-$9D38
; Entry A8/X8 context. Magnitude supplied in DP22/23/24; sign flag DP28 and
; controls DP21 supplied by upstream parser (not reproduced in these tests).
; Repeated subtract/add-back of bank-local24-bit powers at $8221-$822F:
; 100000,10000,1000,100,10. Emits quotient tokens to $0468-$046C, remainder
; OR80 at $046D (final token). Replaces leading zeros in first five positions
; with60. If sign flag set and a preceding blank exists, replaces that position
; with71 and moves starting index back one. Six-digit magnitude with first digit
; nonzero has no leading blank for a minus token; do not promise signed text.
; DP AF=start index; unless ((DP21>>2)&7) nonzero, then AF=6-width modulo256.
; Width7 produces AF=FF; observed arithmetic only, not a safe/legal script width.
; DP B4/B5=0468 points to output tokens; no screen writes in this formatter.
; 1696 cases:53 magnitudes0..999999 (boundaries plus40 seeded values), two sign
; flags, widths0-7, two banks. Compare all six tokens/start/pointer against an
; independent decimal model. No proof for larger24-bit magnitudes, upstream sign
; extension, glyph appearance, or complete numeric command/render timing.
