; 03T. SRAM THREE-SLOT EXPERIMENT -- generated inline payload
; @sram_output_size 4194304
; Version 1: 8 KiB, slots at $0000/$0100/$0200; journal copies +$00/+$80.
; Each record: A5 SN version slot length seq16 packed16 medals16 crc16.
; CRC-16/A001 init FFFF over bytes 1..25; commit byte written last.
; Resume uses native checkpoint reconstruction, selected party and full resources.
; Scratch $70:1F00..1F1F; new code/assets in appended bank $20 only.
; IMPLEMENTED / RUNTIME-EMULATOR: isolated three-slot checkpoint experiment.
; User selected separate Save/Load menus and three slots; no autosaving.
; build_sram.py verifies the original SHA, pads the second MiB with FF,
; then applies these inline recipes. Base bank contents stay allocated.
; Header $00:FFD6..FFD8 changes 00 0A 00 -> 02 0B 03: battery RAM,
; 2 MiB ROM, 8 KiB SRAM. Slow mapper remains20; fast adds all03S bytes.
; LoROM upper ROM windows now extend to $3F/$BF in this companion only.
; New bank20 code is deliberately identical and runs at slow speed in both.
; SRAM mapping used: $70:0000..1FFF; pinned Snes9x exposes8192 bytes.
; No speed/ROM identity is stored in records; raw .srm files interchange.
; Slot stride256; valid record bytes0..27, bytes28..31 reserved/ignored.
; SRAM CAPACITY AUDIT2026-10-11: three256-byte slot regions0000..02FF,
; each with two128-byte journal windows. Record uses28 meaningful bytes:
; header/seq8, progress16, medals2, CRC2. Python represents32 bytes with4
; ignored bytes; each journal window has100 bytes beyond meaningful content,
; or96 beyond32-byte representation. Recovery copies duplicate the payload.
; Reserve entire1F00..1FFF page for menu/03Y working data. Unallocated region
; 0300..1EFF is7168 bytes (7KiB),87.5% of8192. Extra fields need no file growth.
; Extend save/load, length/version and CRC together; retain commit-last journal.
; Read/migrate v1 with defaults, write extended v2; old ROMs reject v2 records.
; Ignored bytes have no initialization/CRC guarantee. Test all slots, migration,
; defaults, corruption and interrupted writes. No format change in this audit.
; Selection validates commit, magic, version, slot, length and CRC.
; Compare sequence modulo65536; ties and half-range ambiguity choose A.
; Save invalidates the alternate copy before writing header/payload/CRC;
; final A5 commits it. Previous valid copy is untouched. Not host-file atomic.
; $01:B785 JSL03C813 -> JSL20:load_entry; native JSR B76B still rebuilds
; stats/checkpoint map and refills resources using startup party selection.
; Load entry copies packed16, unpacks native FIELDS, and restores medals16.
; $02:DF09 JSL03D662 -> JSL20:save_entry; DF0D JSRE575 -> JMP C9C4.
; Save entry packs current mapped fields before writing, without password
; text encoding. B returns to native game menu; native UI closes submenu.
; Four identified menu label strings become LOAD/SAVE, indices unchanged.
; Load menu offers three slots plus original password entry; B also enters
; original keyboard03C813. Empty/damaged slots stay in Load menu.
; Menus show SAVED/EMPTY; A selects, Up/Down wraps, occupied Save asks
; for second A confirmation; B cancels overwrite. A/B dismiss status.
; Entry preserves P, full A/X/Y and DBR, leaves DP unchanged (required0),
; uses M8/X16 and DBR20; binary arithmetic as native caller. Native calls
; and low-WRAM mirror assumptions are exercised with active interrupts.
; Input uses native $7A/$7B edges; persistent scratch is SRAM, not DP.
; New text uses native font and positive NMI CPU stream ($A0=1,$A1..A3).
; Relocated03C826..C89C setup has only long calls/local branches, assets
; remain in bank03; terminal RTS becomes RTL. Original password intact.
; Save state is checkpoint progress, not coordinates, HP/NP or battle state.
; RUNTIME: verify_sram.py runs20 isolated cases; sram_acceptance_results.json
; records current ROM hashes. All3 cross-load in both directions; medals
; exceed255; overwrite decline/commit; valid older-copy recovery for bad CRC,
; invalid commit/version; seq wrap; zero/FF/wrong-slot/version/CRC rejection;
; original controller-entered password succeeds in both; two-player load.
; Save fixtures restore disclosed native-menu snapshots and inject currency/
; medals. Cross-loads cold boot with raw8KiB file in cartridge SRAM.
; Interrupted write is simulated invalid commit, not a physical power cut.
; No full-playthrough, hardware, host-flush or exhaustive-stage certification.
; Manual checklist: Testing/SRAM/README.md. Cold boot; avoid old save states.
; REPORTED user manual test: medals carry over, saving available anywhere
; tested, loading works and resumes at the last convenience center visited.
; REPORTED two-player comparison: slowdown reproduced in SlowROM and not
; seen in FastROM. User accepted unchanged FastROM/SRAM as release0.2.
